        "The line degree and near-split obstruction retain separate Gauduchon tests, rank>=2 and fixed C4 neighborhood.",
        "Regularization requires total-space local positive quadratic margins, not fixed-fiber margins; the example verifies the distinction.",
        "Polar square may be nonsmooth and strongly pseudoconvex G need not be real convex; real strong convexity comes from the Legendre upper Hessian argument.",
        "Potential editorial candidate: convex-root line169 is a long inventory and omits the new negative-curvature subsection; assess only after complete first reader pass.",
        "Hirzebruch quotient incidence exclusions, stable extensions and analytic Dolbeault convergence fit the stated line convention. Walter prioritary-stack theorem remains an explicitly imported external input; its proof is not freshly audited.",
        "Fixed Stein hypersurface uses algebraic frame, Runge and Oka–Weil accepted inputs; countable dilation controls all candidate Finsler metrics.",
        "Projective completion U_E, punctured bundle E minus Z and total space E are distinct domains; compactness is locally waived only in the new negative-weight subsection and explicitly restored by external tensor products.",
        "Nonpositive/flat projective-complement indices and split Hopf pure regimes are exact. Mixed Hopf indices retain lower/upper bounds and remain undetermined.",
        "Potential reader addition: connect compact negative-bundle total-space exhaustion to the later maximal projective-complement index without claiming a new convexity theorem.",
        "Arbitrary-bidegree pluriharmonic support, Kähler pullback mass and continuous heat smoothing retain separate settings; heat flow positivity is repaired by a small Kähler power.",
